    "probe_text": "Here is the full `POST /api/owners` pipeline as the code stands, in execution order. Every top-level step lives in `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`; I've marked each as **[validation]** (can reject) or **[side-effect]** (mutates state / responds). Steps 9 onward all run under `govern: [ transaction ]`, so they commit as one unit at the end.\n\n**Gate (whole endpoint)**\n- **[validation] Security** \u2014 `authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"`. The request is rejected before any step runs unless the caller has `OWNER_ADMIN`.\n\n**Pre-transaction steps**\n\n1. **CheckIdempotencyKey** \u2014 **[side-effect + validation]** Reads the optional `Idempotency-Key` header and publishes an `IdempotencyToken`. If that key already produced an owner, throws `IdempotentReplayException` to replay the stored owner (200) and short-circuit the create.\n2. **RequireOwnerFields** \u2014 **[validation]** Binds `@RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` (the only body read). Requires non-blank `firstName`, `lastName`, `city`, `telephone`, and an address (either `addressLine1` **or** the flat `address`). Missing any \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (400). Publishes the body for later steps.\n3. **NormalizeOwnerTelephone** \u2014 **[side-effect + validation]** Rewrites `telephone` to E.164 in place; if it can't form valid E.164 \u2192 400.\n4. **ValidateTelephoneLength** \u2014 **[validation]** Checks national-number length by country code: `+61` needs 9 digits, `+1` needs 10; wrong length \u2192 400. Other country codes untouched.\n5. **NormalizeOwnerEmail** \u2014 **[side-effect + validation]** Only if an email is present: rejects invalid syntax and disposable domains (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) with `InvalidOwnerEmailException` (400); otherwise lower-cases it in place. Missing email is allowed.\n6. **NormalizeOwnerAddress** \u2014 **[side-effect]** Normalizes address fields in place: trim, collapse internal whitespace, upper-case, expand abbreviations (`ST`\u2192`STREET`, `RD`\u2192`ROAD`, `AVE`\u2192`AVENUE`). Composes the canonical stored `address` from line1 (+ line2), else from the flat `address`.\n7. **ValidatePostcode** \u2014 **[validation]** Only if a postcode is present: must be 4 digits, and for known cities must fall in range (Sydney 2000\u20132099, Melbourne 3000\u20133099, Brisbane 4000\u20134099). Otherwise `InvalidPostcodeException` (400). Unknown cities accept any 4-digit value.\n8. **RejectFutureRegistrationDate** \u2014 **[validation]** If `registrationDate` is present and after the server's today \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` (400).\n\n**Transactional steps (`govern: [ transaction ]`, single commit at the end)**\n\n9. **RejectDuplicateIdentity** \u2014 **[validation]** Rejects (409, `DuplicateIdentityException`) if the full `IdentityKey` (normalized telephone + email + householdId) matches any non-deleted existing owner.\n10. **RejectCityAtCapacity** \u2014 **[validation]** 409 (`CityAtCapacityException`) if the city already holds \u2265 50 owners (compared case-insensitively, whitespace collapsed).\n11. **RejectDailyLimit** \u2014 **[validation]** 429 (`DailyLimitExceededException`) if \u2265 100 owners are already registered for that (business-day-rolled) registration date.\n12. **BuildOwner** \u2014 **[side-effect]** Maps the DTO to an `Owner` entity and sets `registrationDate` to the supplied date (or today), rolled to a business day.\n13. **AssignCustomerCode** \u2014 **[side-effect]** Sets `customerCode` (the memberId) to `V2<region><2-digit fiscal year><8 hex chars of SHA-256(telephone+lastName)><Luhn check digit>`.\n14. **DeduplicateCustomerCode** \u2014 **[side-effect]** If that code already belongs to another owner, appends `-<n>` (smallest `n \u2265 2`) to make it unique.\n15. **AssignHousehold** \u2014 **[side-effect]** Sets `householdId` deterministically from last name + postcode (null when no postcode).\n16. **AssignNamesakeCount** \u2014 **[side-effect]** Sets `namesakeCount` = number of existing owners sharing this first+last name (case-insensitive), counted before save.\n17. **FlagPossibleDuplicate** \u2014 **[side-effect]** Sets `possibleDuplicateOf` to an existing owner with the same postcode and same Soundex(lastName) but a different identity key. Skipped when `sharesHousehold=true` or no postcode; left null if no match.\n18. **SaveOwner** \u2014 **[side-effect]** Persists the owner via `ownerRepository.save`.\n19. **RecordIdempotencyKey** \u2014 **[side-effect]** Builds the `OwnerDto`, applies gold `HouseholdTier`, sets `bulkSignupWarning` and `capacityWarning`, and records the DTO against the idempotency key so a later repeat replays it.\n20. **AuditOwnerCreated** \u2014 **[side-effect]** Emits two `AUDIT` log lines (incrementing a sequence counter), including computed owner segment and membership level.\n21. **NotifyWelcome** \u2014 **[side-effect]** Emits a `NOTIFY` welcome log line for the new owner.\n22. **RespondWithOwnerCreated** \u2014 **[side-effect]** Builds the response DTO, applies gold tier, sets `bulkSignupWarning`, `capacityWarning`, and `riskFlag`, and responds **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\nA few things worth flagging from reading it:\n- The body is bound once (step 2); every later step reads the same mutated `OwnerFieldsDto`/`Owner` via `@Val`, so normalizations in steps 3\u20136 are what the duplicate/household/save logic downstream actually sees.\n- The three duplicate-style helper functions named in the directory (`RejectDuplicateEmail`, `RejectDuplicateTelephone`, `RejectDuplicateHousehold`) are **not** wired into this pipeline \u2014 the single `RejectDuplicateIdentity` (step 9) replaces them, per its own Javadoc.\n- The DTO enrichment (gold tier / warnings) is computed three times independently \u2014 in steps 19, 20 (partially) and 22 \u2014 rather than once."
